cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "repocraft: deterministic Python project scaffolding from a validated spec"
abstract: >-
  repocraft turns a validated YAML spec or a short recipe request into a
  complete Python project: packaging metadata, src layout, tests, lint and
  type-check configuration, CI, CodeQL and Dependabot. The same input and the
  same repocraft version always produce byte-identical output. Two optional
  model-assisted paths exist, and in both the model never writes files
  directly: the ask path validates a strict recipe intent, and the craft path
  verifies a proposed snippet through deterministic gates before anything is
  written.
authors:
  - family-names: "Furox"
    given-names: "Art"
    alias: "Furox-Art"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Furox-Art/repocraft"
url: "https://github.com/Furox-Art/repocraft"
license: MIT
version: 0.4.1
date-released: "2026-10-29"
keywords:
  - project scaffolding
  - deterministic code generation
  - byte-identical output
  - python
  - reproducibility
  - developer tools
